Spec: Bounded lexical JSON

Purpose:
  Preserve exact JSON token distinctions and Unicode scalar validity before contract semantics are evaluated.

Owns:
  ./StrictJson.java

References:
  /docs/adr/0001-public-contract-normalization.md

Must:
  Decode UTF-8 without replacement and reject duplicate decoded keys, invalid surrogate pairs and non-JSON syntax.
  Bound input bytes, nested containers and value count before allocating an unbounded parse tree.
  Preserve numeric lexical form through @StrictJson.NumberToken so semantic integer checks can reject decimals and exponents.
  Write valid normalized JSON without altering valid string contents.
  Optionally capture the original control manifest value slice without changing ordinary parse behavior.
  Capture the original root connection policy slice for request parsing so whitespace and escaped encoding count toward the same policy byte limit on both platforms.
  Preserve the original root control params slice for formal open dispatch so envelope parsing cannot erase nested policy byte limits.

Must not:
  Coerce an invalid input into a plausible declaration.

Done when:
  The shared malformed encoding, escaped-key, nesting and lexical-number cases retain their expected outcomes.
